# Event Creation Template
```typescript
await calendar.events.insert({
  calendarId: staff.googleCalendarId,
  resource: {
    summary: title,
    location: patient.fullAddress,
    description: buildDescription(appointment, staff.staff_type),
    start: { dateTime: startISO, timeZone: 'Asia/Dubai' },
    end: { dateTime: endISO, timeZone: 'Asia/Dubai' }
  }
});
```

# Driver vs Medical Description
- If `staff_type === "driver"` → call `buildDriverDescription`
- Else → `buildMedicalDescription`

## Event Title Format
```typescript
const buildEventTitle = (appointment: Appointment, staff: Staff[]) => {
  const patientFirst = appointment.patient.first_name;
  const area = appointment.area;
  const type = appointment.type;
  const staffFirsts = staff.map(s => s.first_name).join(', ');
  
  return `${patientFirst} - ${area} - ${type} - ${staffFirsts}`;
};
```

## Timezone Handling
- Always use `Asia/Dubai` timezone
- Store all timestamps in UTC in database
- Convert to local timezone for display
- Use `date-fns-tz` for timezone conversions

## Webhook Handling
```typescript
// Handle Google Calendar webhook
app.post('/api/webhooks/calendar', async (req, res) => {
  const { event } = req.body;
  
  if (event.updated) {
    await updateAppointmentFromCalendar(event);
  }
  
  res.status(200).send('OK');
});
```

## Calendar Sync Patterns
- Bidirectional sync between database and Google Calendar
- Handle conflicts by prioritizing database state
- Use event IDs to track sync status
- Implement retry logic for failed operations
